From: telegram.tools rich-message renderer
Subject: [PATCH] Add TDESKTOP_RENDERER_HARNESS hook for the sessionless
 renderer targets

The only in-tree change the renderer needs: an opt-in add_subdirectory()
hook so the harness targets (renderer/cpp) configure inside the pinned
tree with access to tdesktop::td_iv / tdesktop::td_ui and the desktop-app
cmake helpers. Off by default; upstream behavior is unchanged unless
-DTDESKTOP_RENDERER_HARNESS_DIR=<path to renderer/cpp> is passed.

Applied at build time by renderer/scripts/build-native.sh; never committed
to the submodule.
---
--- a/Telegram/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/Telegram/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -44,6 +44,10 @@ if (DESKTOP_APP_TEST_APPS)
     include(cmake/tests.cmake)
 endif()

+if (TDESKTOP_RENDERER_HARNESS_DIR)
+    add_subdirectory(${TDESKTOP_RENDERER_HARNESS_DIR} ttr-renderer)
+endif()
+
 if (WIN32)
     include(cmake/generate_midl.cmake)
     generate_midl(Telegram ${src_loc}
